buildQuiz("temp-anomaly-quiz", "Check Your Understanding — Temperature Trends", [
  {
    q: "Based on the Global Temperature Anomaly chart, what overall pattern is visible from 1880 to 2024?",
    options: [
      "A) Temperatures have remained flat",
      "B) Temperatures gradually decreased",
      "C) Temperatures show a clear warming trend, especially after 1980",
      "D) Temperatures peaked in 1940 and then declined"
    ],
    correct: 2,
    explanation: "The chart shows mostly negative anomalies before 1980 and a rapid rise to over +1°C by 2024, indicating accelerating warming."
  },
  {
    q: "Around what decade did global temperature anomalies begin staying consistently above the baseline (0°C)?",
    options: [
      "A) The 1920s",
      "B) The 1940s",
      "C) The 1980s",
      "D) The 2000s"
    ],
    correct: 2,
    explanation: "The 1980s mark the point where anomalies consistently stayed above 0°C and continued climbing, reflecting the acceleration of human-caused warming."
  }
])

20.1 Part 1: The Invisible Engine
Climate change begins with the atmosphere’s chemistry. To understand why the Earth is warming, we must first look at the “Keeling Curve,” the most famous graph in Earth Science.
